\paragraph{Detector calibration matters more than accuracy.}
Replacing the calibrated discriminative TF-IDF+LR (ECE\,=\,0.048) with uncalibrated generative perplexity detectors reverses the advantage even at comparable AUC (GPT-2 PPL: AUC\,=\,0.91, $\Delta{=}{+}0.096$; N-gram PPL: AUC\,=\,0.73, $\Delta{=}{+}0.126$; single seed, $\tau{=}0.8$; Appendix~\ref{app:detector}).
